icans  this is uh this is a complex question  that requires a lot of different  um exploration and the answer is not  um because white people are merely  racist  and they vote for republicans that  that's not if that's what you believe  it's overly simplistic there are of  course elements of racism  uh but that's really not what this is  about so it is true that when you  look at current polling and you slice  and dice it demographically by age by  race  by income you know all these different  things by education donald trump is  winning among men by not not by a huge  margin donald trump is winning among  white  voters and donald trump is winning among  uneducated voters the more education you  have the more likely  you are to support joe biden the answer  to a lot of the white  support for republicans actually is  religion and i want people to be very  very carefully  understanding what it is that i'm saying  here white  evangelicals overwhelmingly vote for  republicans  white non-evangelicals are pretty split  between the democratic and the  republican party so to say it another  way  were it not for white evangelicals  the republican party would not have the  advantage it has  among white voters and this is why you  might  see american politics and you say  there's more support for abortion today  than there has been at any time since  roe v wade  uh and yet they st the republicans still  kowtow to being against abortion  and they still uh try to play you know  they trump speaking at the march for  life and all of this different stuff  the reason why is that they are  dependent  on the white evangelical voter not only  for votes but also for  donations evangelicals are just over a  third of white voters  okay so you've got all white voters a  third of white voters are evangelical  they voted for trump roughly four to one  80 to 20.  other white voters went for hillary  56-44 according to exit polls against  trump in 2016.  so when you slice and dice the  elector